/ersummoneditor
/cmd/ersummoneditor/ersummoneditor
/cmd/ersummoneditorgui/ersummoneditorgui
/dist/
*.tmp
coverage.out

# Compiled test binaries. `go test -c` drops one of these beside the package
# and a 17 MB gio.test once rode into a commit that way.
*.test

# Drawing prompts the retired tools/artbriefs wrote (2026-09-23): local,
# untracked, left in place rather than deleted.
artwork/prompts/

# artwork/ is the bench, not the shelf. Candidates for creatures still being
# drawn sit here flat, one file per attempt; the moment one is chosen it moves
# to internal/ui/gio/assets/entities/<model>.png and the rest of that
# creature's attempts go. Nothing here ships, so none of it is tracked.
artwork/*.png

# The accepted art at full resolution: 3 MB a file and 849 MB once the roster
# is complete, which is not something to put in a repository. tools/artpack
# packs these down to the 128px icons the editor embeds, and THOSE are tracked.
# Back these up somewhere - an AI image cannot be regenerated.
artwork/masters/

# Pictures downloaded from ChatGPT on their way in (tools/artqueue): the
# batch being drawn, its review page, and every download already filed, kept
# in inbox/taken. artwork/queue.csv, which says what each one is, is tracked.
artwork/inbox/

# Contact sheets: every variant's picture beside its name, made to review the
# pictures by eye. Remade at will, never shipped.
artwork/sheets/

# Compiled command binaries dropped beside the repo root by `go build ./tools/...`.
# One of these - a 6.9 MB tools/batchtest build - was committed by accident in
# e990e32 and rebuilt into another commit before anyone noticed.
/batchtest
